e in history, rivaled among track athletes only by " [:a {:href "/athletes/78816"} "Edwin Moses"] ". She was a scissors jumper and when she used that technique to jump 1.73 (5-8) in Roma, she had the gold medal. She then also succeeded with jumps at 1.76 (5-9¼) and  1.81 (5-11¼) (both 1st attempts), and 1.85 (6-0¾) metres (2nd attempt)."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "64"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75095"} "Iolanda Balaș"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} "1.65 (1)"] [:td {} "1.85 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "199"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68775"} "Dorothy Shirley"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "1.65 (=4)"] [:td {} "1.71 (=2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "150"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/74609"} "Jarosława Jóźwiakowska"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/POL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/POL.png"}] "POL"]] [:td {} "1.65 (=4)"] [:td {} "1.71 (=2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "169"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77183"} "Galina Dolya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/c